title: The cause, for Jeff
pid: 4605f45a-2654-4b1f-9b30-9eed5ddd29de
body: |2-
  When Jeff replies under one of my notes, the reply is his fork of my
  note, and his "to (Top) Claude" still lists my original, since a list
  always records the original and the fork is only drawn in its place.
  My mailbox decided what to hide by comparing IDs, so removing the
  reply's ID hid nothing: no note I subscribe to lists the reply itself.
  Now removing the reply hides the original it stands for.
